{title: 537 - He Leadeth Me}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #537 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 537}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]He leadeth me: O [F]blessed thought!
O [C]words with heavenly comfort [G]fraught!
What[C]e’er I do, wher[F]e’er I be,
Still [C]’tis God’s [Am]hand that [G]leadeth [C]me.
He leadeth [G]me, [G7]He [C]lead[F]eth [C]me,
[F]By [C]His own [Am]hand He [C]leadeth [G]me;
[G7]His [C]faithful [G]fol[G7]lower [C]I [F]would [C]be,
[F]For [C]by His [Am]hand He [G]leadeth [C]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C]He leadeth me, [F]he leadeth me,
[C]by his own [G]hand he leadeth me;
[C]his faithful follower [F]I would be,
[C]for [Am]by his [G]hand he [C]leadeth me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Sometimes mid scenes [F]of deepest gloom,
[C]sometimes where [G]Eden's bowers bloom,
[C]by waters still, [F]o'er troubled sea,
[C]still [Am]'tis his [G]hand that [C]leadeth me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Lord, I would place [F]my hand in thine,
[C]nor ever [G]murmur nor repine;
[C]content, whatever [F]lot I see,
[C]since [Am]'tis my [G]God that [C]leadeth me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]And when my task [F]on earth is done,
[C]when by thy [G]grace the victory's won,
[C]e'en death's cold wave [F]I will not flee,
[C]since [Am]God through [G]Jordan [C]leadeth me.
{end_of_verse}
